  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Marking most of your vrchat world as static can be a big performance boost, but since it's \"invisible\" beyond the performance gain, it's very easy for this step to just slip a creator's mind.   The SDK should show a warning if it detects that nothing at all in the scene has been marked static; there's no good way to tell *which* gameobjects need it, but the odds of a vrchat world existing in which absolutely NOTHING could be marked static, seems so low that it seems reasonable for this to be sufficient cause to remind the user to at least look into it before submitting the final version of their world.",
